---
// Pearl › 07 — Handoff: label, headline, two paragraphs side by side, then the docs panel.
//
// The panel is a 975 × 607.6 canvas (`--u` is one Figma pixel) scaled to the column width,
// like First Move: the hero artwork blurred as a backdrop on the slide fill, a badge
// documentation page on the left and a header-rules page running off the bottom right.
// Figma's two screenshot shadows are normalised to shadow-media (DESIGN.md › Elevation).
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Section from './Section.astro';
import backdrop from '../../assets/images/pearl/01_hero__frame-1853320970.png';
import badgeDocs from '../../assets/images/pearl/15_section-07-handoff__image-139.png';
import headerRules from '../../assets/images/pearl/16_section-07-handoff__image-154.png';
---

<Section tone="pearl" width="wide" labelledby="handoff-title">
  <div class="heading">
    <p class="text-label-m label">Handoff</p>
    <h2 id="handoff-title">Packaging a system to outlive the project</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="columns text-body-xl">
    <p>
      Each core component got a documentation page in Figma, covering its anatomy, its states and
      the tokens it pulls from, so Pearl could be picked up by someone who hadn’t built it. But one
      question had followed me from the start. Every UI we designed was linked to Pearl in our
      Figma, so how would the system move to the client without breaking those links? I left it
      until the end of the project, and I’d likely answer it earlier next time.
    </p>
    <p class="text-body-l-mobile">
      When the time came, I asked Claude for options and went with Figma’s own move-file and
      library-swap features, the cleanest and safest of them. The tutorials made it look like a
      few clicks, but with a system this size, it wasn’t. The foundations and icon library swapped
      across easily, while the component library stalled Figma for about an hour and a half, and a
      few components needed fixing by hand. In total, moving every library took about two days. By
      the end, Pearl was fully settled in the client’s Figma environment, ready for whoever picks
      it up next.
    </p>
  </div>

  <figure class="figure">
    <div class="panel">
      <Image class="backdrop" src={backdrop} alt="" widths={[975, 1950]} sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 975px, 100vw" />
      <Image
        class="shot badge-docs"
        src={badgeDocs}
        alt="Pearl's badge documentation in Figma: an Order Details card with status badges, and the Do guidelines for using them."
        widths={[550, 906]}
        sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 550px, 60vw"
      />
      <Image
        class="shot header-rules"
        src={headerRules}
        alt="Pearl's header rules documentation: a bottom sheet titled Unlimited Gaming, marked Title is required, with the rules listed below."
        widths={[896, 1624]}
        sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 896px, 95vw"
      />
    </div>
  </figure>
</Section>

<style>
  /* Figma gaps 20, snapped to 24. */
  .heading {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
  }

  .label {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  /* Balanced so it wraps over two even lines rather than leaving "project" alone. */
  h2 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-40);
    margin-top: var(--space-24);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Figma gap 60, snapped to 56. Panel fills the 972 column (Figma 975, 3px over). */
  .figure {
    margin-top: var(--space-56);
    container-type: inline-size;
  }

  .panel {
    --u: calc(100cqw / 975);
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 975 / 607.6;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background-color: var(--pearl-slide-bg);
  }

  /* Full width, 608 tall, centred vertically, blurred 50. */
  .backdrop {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 50%;
    translate: 0 -50%;
    width: 100%;
    height: calc(608 * var(--u));
    object-fit: cover;
    filter: blur(calc(50 * var(--u)));
  }

  .shot {
    position: absolute;
    max-width: none;
    object-fit: cover;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-media);
  }

  /* 550 × 450, 44 from the left, centred 48 above the middle. */
  .badge-docs {
    left: calc(44 * var(--u));
    top: calc(30.8 * var(--u));
    width: calc(550 * var(--u));
    height: calc(450 * var(--u));
  }

  /* 896 × 508 at 534 / 201.8, running off the right and bottom edges. */
  .header-rules {
    left: calc(534 * var(--u));
    top: calc(201.8 * var(--u));
    width: calc(896 * var(--u));
    height: calc(508 * var(--u));
  }

  /* Tablet: the paragraphs stack. */
  @media (max-width: 1199px) {
    .columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-24);
    }
  }

  /* Mobile: smaller corners so the scaled-down panel keeps its proportions. */
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .figure {
      margin-top: var(--space-40);
    }

    .panel {
      border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    }
  }
</style>
